The potential vulnerability is related to Insecure Permissions. This vulnerability arises because the code intends to save a file with restricted access ("accessible only by the current user") but does not explicitly define or enforce these permissions during file creation. If the underlying operating system or file system defaults to broader permissions, or if the code fails to correctly set the file mode bits, the file could become accessible to other users on the system, compromising the confidentiality of the "secret" data.

